7. Linear vs non-linear, CR_I vs CR_O, sensitivity (random inputs on 1..a_BW)
====================================================================================================
  n = 4..7, 400 inputs: same criterion ranks, ties within 1e-5 (linear vs midpoint of non-linear intervals) 104/400; linear w inside every non-linear interval 35/400; max |w_lin - midpoint| median 0.050, 90th pct 0.087
    of these, the 71 with CR_I under the threshold: same ranks 36/71, max |w_lin - midpoint| median 0.041, 90th pct 0.081
  400 inputs (a_BW >= 3, n 3..9): over threshold by CR_I 261, by CR_O 279; same verdict 323
  one judgement moved by +-1 (within 1..a_BW): weights unchanged in 916/3697 moves (25 %, the "low sensitivity" of Ratandhara & Kumar Corollary 1)

