8. Edge cases
====================================================================================================
  n = 2, a_BW = 3: w [0.7500, 0.2500] xi 0.0; (a_BW/(1+a_BW), 1/(1+a_BW)) = [0.7500, 0.2500]
  all ones (a_BW = 1): w [0.2500, 0.2500, 0.2500, 0.2500] xi 0.0, CR_I 0.0 -> equal weights
  a_BW = 1 but a_B2 = 9 (entry above a_BW): w [0.5758, 0.0909, 0.3333] xi 0.2424; CR_I 0.0 (Liang Eq. 7 sets CR_I = 0 whenever a_BW = 1: the inconsistency is invisible -> cap entries at a_BW)
  a_BW = 2, n = 3, bo [1, 2, 2] ow [2, 2, 1]: CR_I 1.000, threshold 0.0 (Liang footnote 2: any CR_I > 0 is "revise"); Excel solver shows no threshold (VLOOKUP starts at 3)
  B over j and j over W both 4 with a_BW = 9 (4 x 4 = 16 != 9): CR_I 0.097, suggested fix for j: a_jW = a_BW / a_Bj = 2.25 -> 2 (CR_I_j 0.014)
  n =  2: BWM asks 2n - 3 =  1 judgements, AHP n(n - 1)/2 =   1
  n =  3: BWM asks 2n - 3 =  3 judgements, AHP n(n - 1)/2 =   3
  n =  5: BWM asks 2n - 3 =  7 judgements, AHP n(n - 1)/2 =  10
  n =  9: BWM asks 2n - 3 = 15 judgements, AHP n(n - 1)/2 =  36
  n = 15: BWM asks 2n - 3 = 27 judgements, AHP n(n - 1)/2 = 105

